Time steps, CFL stability and temporal accuracy (@fd-time-stepping: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/CFD-Verification-and-Validation-NPARC.lingua#r_7P72ZWZEJ0SVMWFDGK52N9AZPV", #source "../sources/Computational-Fluid-Dynamics-Vermeire-Pereira-Karbasian.lingua#r_7B08DEGENZD4JFFRFNPKJCVFCW", #source "../sources/Notes-on-CFD-Greenshields-Weller.lingua#r_50W8G5SX00YH7R6TBXK4FAP5MY", #fluid-dynamics "../../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8") { r_60M0VT0DEYA3P6E9DC371K6PQT
**Read:** [CFD verification and validation — NPARC Alliance](../sources/CFD-Verification-and-Validation-NPARC.lingua#r_7P72ZWZEJ0SVMWFDGK52N9AZPV), temporal convergence; [Computational Fluid Dynamics: An Open-Source Approach — Vermeire and colleagues](../sources/Computational-Fluid-Dynamics-Vermeire-Pereira-Karbasian.lingua#r_7B08DEGENZD4JFFRFNPKJCVFCW), time integration and solver controls; [Notes on Computational Fluid Dynamics — Greenshields and Weller](../sources/Notes-on-CFD-Greenshields-Weller.lingua#r_50W8G5SX00YH7R6TBXK4FAP5MY), transient algorithms and stability.

The Courant number relates a propagation speed and time step to a spatial scale; for gas or shallow-water systems the relevant speed includes wave propagation, not only advection. Diffusive and reactive terms can introduce other restrictions. A stability limit belongs to the specific discrete scheme and equation set.

Implicit stepping can relax some stability restrictions while retaining temporal truncation error and nonlinear-solve requirements. Separate physical time advancement from pseudo-time iteration toward a steady state. In transient turbulence or oscillation, sampling every many time steps can impose an additional observation limit even if integration itself is sufficiently resolved.

Refine time step with spatial error controlled, comparing phase, amplitude, integral balances and an event time. Track nonlinear and linear convergence tolerances so incomplete solves do not dominate the refinement result. Test whether adaptive stepping preserves the desired diagnostics and deterministic reproducibility for the stated calculation.

